---
const graphComposeUrl = 'https://github.com/DemchaAV/GraphCompose';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/DemchaAV/graphcompose-ai-flow';
---
<section class="gc" id="graphcompose">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 · the target language</p>
    <h2>GraphCompose is the compile target. The AI learns to speak it.</h2>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <a href={graphComposeUrl}><code>GraphCompose</code></a> is a Java library for
          building PDFs out of <em>semantic primitives</em>: sections, rows, tables,
          themes, layer stacks, shape containers, layout snapshots, and visual regression
          checks. It treats documents as composable nodes, not as a canvas of coordinates.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="accent">This project is the AI workflow that targets GraphCompose
          as a compile target.</strong> The agent receives a visual reference and
          reconstructs it using GraphCompose primitives. The output is not a one-shot
          PDF &mdash; it is a maintainable Java template you can read, diff, and revise.
        </p>
        <p class="meta">
          GraphCompose <code>1.6.0</code> is resolved through JitPack as
          <code>com.github.DemchaAV:GraphCompose:v1.6.0</code>. The skill packs under
          <a href={`${repoUrl}/tree/main/skills/versions`}><code>skills/versions/</code></a>
          are versioned contracts between the agent and a specific GraphCompose API.
        </p>
      </div>

      <pre class="snippet" aria-label="Two paradigms for AI-generated PDFs"><span class="line muted"># artist paradigm</span>
<span class="line warn">canvas.moveTo(72, 720);</span>
<span class="line warn">canvas.drawString("INVOICE");</span>
<span class="line warn">canvas.rect(72, 600, 460, 80);</span>
<span class="line muted">  one-shot. unreviewable.</span>

<span class="line muted"># compiler paradigm (this project)</span>
<span class="line good">Section.of(invoiceHeader)</span>
<span class="line good">    .withTheme(BusinessTheme.mint())</span>
<span class="line good">    .row(invoiceMeta, invoiceTotal)</span>
<span class="line good">    .table(lineItems, spec);</span>
<span class="line muted">  typed. testable. revisable.</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 18px 0;
  }
  .prose strong {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose .accent {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose em {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-style: normal;
  }
  .prose code {
    color: var(--fg);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 0.92rem !important;
    color: var(--fg-dim) !important;
  }

  .snippet {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .line {
    display: block;
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }
  .warn {
    color: #f87171;
  }
  .good {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
